{"ts": 1789782809.936994, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted specification:** Long features **28, 1, and 27** (equal weight, all positive sign).\n**In-sample Sharpe:** 1.302 \u00b7 **Predicted OOS Sharpe:** 0.88 \u00b1 0.32\n\n### How I got there\n1. **Screened all 40 features individually.** Feature 28 was the standout at 1.112 \u2014 more than 1.8\u00d7 the next best. Features 1 (0.606), 12-negated (0.575), and 27 (0.539) formed a second tier; the remaining ~30 features clustered near zero.\n2. **Tested pairs**, which confirmed 28 as the backbone \u2014 every strong pair contained it.\n3. **Tested triples**, converging on a cluster of three near-identical specs all built from 28 plus two of {1, 12neg, 27}.\n4. **Verified sign robustness** by deliberately inverting each component.\n\n### Key judgments\n**The signal looks genuine.** Inverting feature 28's sign collapses the Sharpe from 1.302 to 0.017; inverting 1 or 27 costs ~0.6\u20130.7. Noise-fitted specs don't exhibit that kind of sharp directional structure. The combination gains are also *modest* in the right way \u2014 three signals of 1.11, 0.61, and 0.54 combining to only 1.30 is consistent with diversifying real independent signals, not with overfitting to residuals.\n\n**But the headline number is inflated.** Two separate reasons drove my 0.4 haircut:\n- *Selection bias:* I took the maximum over ~70 evaluations. At n=5000, the standard error on an annualized Sharpe is ~0.22, so max-picking over correlated candidates inflates the estimate by roughly 0.1\u20130.2.\n- *Structural decay:* feature-return relationships drift, and the equal-weight scheme was implicitly tuned to this sample.\n\n**The \"winner\" is arbitrary.** The top three triples spanned just 1.286\u20131.302 \u2014 a gap far below the ~0.22 estimation error. I explicitly did *not* treat 28+1+27 as truly best; it's a coin flip among near-equivalents, broken only by a weak preference for un-inverted signals. This is also why my stated SD is wide (0.32): the honest uncertainty here is dominated not by which of the tied specs I chose, but by how much of feature 28's standalone edge survives contact with new data."}
